<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Limbin Confederacy</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Limbin Confederacy was an alliance of Shan princes formed in the mid-1880s to oppose King <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/thibaw-min">Thibaw</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/burma">Burma</a> and to put a rival prince, the Limbin Prince, on the throne. Its leading members included the saophas of Mongnai and Lawksawk. After the British conquered <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/upper-burma">Upper Burma</a> in 1885 the confederacy resisted British authority, but its leaders submitted in 1887 and the Shan states became British <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/protectorate">protectorates</a>.</p></div>
